# PII scan allowlist.
#
# One literal string per line. Matching text is removed from a file's content
# BEFORE the PII patterns are applied, so an allowlisted string cannot mask a
# real finding elsewhere in the same file - only the exact string is exempt.
#
# Only PUBLIC INSTITUTIONAL contact details belong here: a government agency's
# published phone number, a school's admissions email. Never a person.
#
# Every entry needs a reason on the line above it. An allowlist without reasons
# becomes a place people quietly park things they did not want to deal with,
# and it is the first file to check when the hook stops catching anything.
#
# This allowlist only affects the low-severity tier in practice. An SSN or a
# credential blocks regardless, and neither belongs in this repo at all - not
# even inside a private path. Credentials belong in the password manager.
#
# Example:
#   # National contact centre, published on the agency's own website
#   800-555-0100

